## LEAD 1: Seller Data Hub Public Registry + CORS ACAC Reflection

**Asset:** `api.obi.com/trx-api/fulfillmentsellersteering/seller-data-hub-service/api/v1/public/`

| Gate | Answer |
|------|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — `api.obi.com` is OBI-owned infrastructure under "all company-owned infrastructure" |
| Q2 Reachable | YES — Unauthenticated, public, `/public/` tree responds 200 to any origin |
| Q3 Impact | YES — Full seller registry (imprint, settings, bio certs) enumerable across 6 countries (DE/AT/IT/PL/FR/ES); CORS `ACAC:true` on arbitrary Origin enables cross-origin exfil; feature-toggle exposes 15 internal SOA.* flags |
| Q4 Provable | YES — GET `/public/de/seller-side-panel/{trxId}` returns 200+JSON; boundary oracle confirmed (0→404, 100551→200); OPTIONS with `Origin: https://evil.example` returns `ACAO: https://evil.example` + `ACAC: true` |
| Q5 Novel | YES — Gate divergence proven: 7 sibling services + own `/api/v1/` mirror all return 401 mule-realm; only `/public/` is open |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | YES — Not on out-of-scope list; not DoS, not disclosure of customer/employee/financial data during testing |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | YES — Real misconfig with clear PoC, not a scanner artifact |

**Verdict: VALID**

**Proof steps:** `curl -I 'https://api.obi.com/trx-api/fulfillmentsellersteering/seller-data-hub-service/api/v1/public/de/seller-side-panel/100551'` → 200 + JSON imprint data. `curl -I -H 'Origin: https://evil.example' 'https://api.obi.com/trx-api/fulfillmentsellersteering/seller-data-hub-service/api/v1/public/de/feature-toggle'` → 200 + `ACAO: https://evil.example` + `ACAC: true`.

**Impact:** MEDIUM — Seller PII (imprint, company data) enumerable without auth; any-origin cross-origin reads confirmed. No customer payment/auth data exposed.

**CVSS 3.1:** 5.3 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N) — Information disclosure + CORS misconfiguration.

**Reporting channel:** bugs.olivermaicher.eu — report already materialized at `reports/report-seller-data-hub-public.md`.

---

## LEAD 2: MuleSoft Exchange Portal — Unauthenticated Full API Catalog + S3 Signed URLs

**Asset:** `api.obi.com` (MuleSoft Exchange portal)

| Gate | Answer |
|------|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — `api.obi.com` is OBI-owned |
| Q2 Reachable | YES — Publicly accessible, no auth required, CORS `*` |
| Q3 Impact | YES — Full JSON catalog of 4 marketplace APIs (Product, Price, Inventory, Order Invoice Management) with S3 signed download URLs containing temp AWS credentials; internal org naming exposed (`trx-fulfillmentsellersteering`) |
| Q4 Provable | YES — GET `https://api.obi.com/` returns embedded JSON catalog; S3 URLs extractable without JS |
| Q5 Novel | Partially — MuleSoft Exchange portals are *designed* to be public developer portals; the finding is that OBI's instance exposes internal org structure and S3 temp credentials |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | BORDERLINE — "Disclosure of known public files or directories" + "Outdated software" are always-rejected; however, embedded AWS temp credentials in S3 signed URLs is not "known public files" — it's unintended credential exposure |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | BORDERLINE — A strict triager may reject this as "MuleSoft Exchange is a public developer portal by design." However, the S3 signed URL with embedded AWS temp creds elevates it beyond "public docs" |

**Verdict: HOLD**

**Reason:** MuleSoft Exchange portals are intentionally public; however, embedded AWS temporary credentials in S3 signed download URLs may constitute an information disclosure beyond intended portal scope. Needs program owner judgment on whether public-by-design developer portal content is in scope.

**If accepted:** CVSS 3.1: 5.3 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N). Reporting channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu.

